than the tropics, but that does not mean it always had little food. A warm forest may contain thousands of edible species

35
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:32,000
scattered through dense vegetation. A northern grassland may contain fewer species, yet place a herd containing

36
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:40,000
several tons of meat directly on the horizon. For a skilled hunter, abundance did not need variety. It needed hooves.

37
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Migratory herds were especially valuable because their movement could be predicted. Reindeer follow seasonal routes. Horses and bison gather where

38
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:56,000
grazing is favorable. Rivers, valleys, crossings, cliffs, and narrow passages turn a vast landscape into a series of

39
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:06,000
recurring opportunities. A group that learned those routes did not wander randomly through whiteness. It moved through a map made of animal behavior.

40
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:12,000
That knowledge could transform risk. Arrive too late and the herd is gone.

41
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Arrive at the correct crossing with prepared weapons, enough hunters, and a plan, and the landscape delivers food,

42
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:29,000
hides, senue, bone, antler, and fat in one event. This is the first reason people entered the north. The animals

43
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:36,000
