45,000 years ago. That evidence is striking, but a butchered mammoth is not the same as a town. It may record a

118
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:39,000
brief expedition, a small population, or occupation that left few other traces.

119
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:48,000
The safer conclusion is that humans could penetrate astonishingly far north earlier than once believed. The record becomes firmer later. This difference

120
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:55,000
matters because entering, occupying, and permanently populating a region are separate achievements.

121
00:15:55,000 --> 00:16:02,000
A hunting party can travel into dangerous territory during a favorable season. A community can return repeatedly while retreating south during

122
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:09,000
severe periods. A population can maintain yearround occupation only when its complete system survives the worst

123
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:18,000
weeks. Not the nicest afternoon archaeologists can imagine. Northern colonization probably passed through these stages repeatedly. Seasonal

124
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:30,000
